# Nobody has written a type in this file. The two names read off `request` are those of one record of the program, and that inferred word stood in the guard of both functions. What arrives at the first
# has been through JSON: an ordinary object with the same names, which is no record of the program: the guard failed at every call and every call ran the slow version. A record that only the names
# suggest is no word for a guard: the body asks where it reads and has its other way. It goes by the function's own text: at the second function the record itself is seen to arrive, and it is compiled as
# the first is: what the callers in sight happen to hand over decides nothing.
# f1 = weighUnseen, f2 = weighSeen
# RUN: plan units mechanisms=all
# CHECK-NOT: unit f1:ParameterGuard
# RUN(SEEN): plan units mechanisms=all
# SEEN-NOT: unit f2:ParameterGuard
# RUN(ASKS): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# ASKS-LABEL: code f2:Body
# ASKS: = ShapeTest
